## Key Production Decisions Explained

| Concern | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **JWT Validation** | Resource Server mode with `issuer-uri` only | Spring auto-configures JWKS fetch, key rotation, signature + `iss`/`exp` validation. No hand-rolled decoder. |
| **JWKS Warm-up** | `ApplicationRunner` triggers a fetch on boot | Avoids cold-start latency on first request after deploy. |
| **Header Stripping** | Global filter + `default-filters` in YAML | Prevents header-injection attacks where clients forge `X-User-Id` etc. |
| **Rate Limiting** | Redis-backed `RedisRateLimiter` keyed by JWT `sub` | Per-user throttling, survives restarts, works in clustered deployments. |
| **Circuit Breakers** | Resilience4j with fallback URIs | Prevents cascading failures; returns graceful 503 JSON when downstream is down. |
| **Error Handling** | `ErrorWebExceptionHandler` with `@Order(-2)` | Catches all errors before Spring's default handler; returns consistent JSON. |
| **Stateless** | `NoOpServerSecurityContextRepository` | No HTTP sessions; fully stateless, horizontally scalable. |
| **Graceful Shutdown** | `server.shutdown: graceful` | Lets in-flight requests complete before pod termination. |
| **CORS** | `CorsWebFilter` with allowed origin patterns | Explicit allowlist; no wildcard origins in production. |
| **Observability** | Actuator + Prometheus + structured JSON logs | Metrics, health checks, and trace IDs on every request. |

