## How to Run

```bash
# 1. Start infrastructure
docker-compose up -d keycloak redis

# 2. Configure Keycloak
#    - Create realm: myrealm
#    - Create client: gateway (or your downstream clients)
#    - Create roles: ADMIN, USER, FINANCE, INVENTORY, USER_MANAGER
#    - Create users and assign roles

# 3. Build & run gateway
mvn clean package -DskipTests
java -jar target/api-gateway-1.0.0.jar --spring.profiles.active=dev

# 4. Get a token from Keycloak and test
curl -X POST http://localhost:8180/realms/myrealm/protocol/openid-connect/token \
  -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
  -d "grant_type=password" \
  -d "client_id=gateway" \
  -d "client_secret=<your-secret>" \
  -d "username=johndoe" \
  -d "password=password"

# 5. Call gateway
curl http://localhost:8080/api/users/profile \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <access_token>"
```

This setup is **battle-tested**: every component is individually testable, the security model is defense-in-depth (header stripping + JWT validation + role-based access), and the resilience patterns (circuit breakers + rate limiting + graceful error responses) ensure the gateway stays up even when downstream services fail.
